    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1105">

                <pb facs="0934" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/16664.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of Texas to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austin, Texas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-02T12:15:00-06:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 2, 1915—12.15 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Replying to your favor October 30 beg to advise that you will receive my hearty
                    cooperation along the lines suggested for quieting border conditions. Have given
                    your telegram widespread advertisement and have asked the cooperation of
                    everybody in carrying out the policy suggested by you.</p>
                <p>Thanking you [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. E. Ferguson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
